content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line (chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite)",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 7.1 mm/s RMS at the drive-end housing sits exactly on the Zone C/Zone D boundary of HF-300 Figure 3. Zone C (4.5-7.1) is 'Restricted - plan maintenance' and Zone D (7.1-11.0) is 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The figure does not say which zone a value on the boundary belongs to. Because Zone D cannot be ruled out, treat the reading conservatively as Zone D, the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The site rule says vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone means stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. With the conservative Zone D reading, this rule applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature of 72 C is above the manufacturer's normal limit (up to 70 C) but below the alarm limit (80 C) and the trip limit (90 C). The site P1 rule for temperature (above the manufacturer's alarm limit) is not triggered by temperature alone. The temperature is elevated, so check for bearing wear or over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leak was reported, so the troubleshooting symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal' does not apply and seal replacement is not indicated by this report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear: this is consistent with both high vibration and above-normal bearing housing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment: this is consistent with both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing: this is a listed cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage: this is a listed cause of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation: this is a listed cause of high vibration. Check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-103 immediately and notify the reliability engineer. Do not restart without the reliability engineer's agreement.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump, apply the required isolations: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves; a line-break permit, draining and venting first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Take vibration readings on both bearing housings (drive end and non-drive end) and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Use the readings taken before the pump was stopped if available.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the bearing grease quantity for over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and the impeller for wear, damage or imbalance, and check NPSH for cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end bearing 6312-C3 and non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg and needs lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. If the seal is disturbed, this serial must use cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, with a gland nut torque of 30 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm. Tighten all other fasteners to Table 5 of the manual.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or the bearing housing, re-align with the laser tool to 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart is authorised, re-measure vibration on both housings. Confirm the highest reading is below Zone D and that housing temperature is within the normal range (70 C or lower).",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Replace as a pair with HF3-510 if wear is found.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Replace as a pair with HF3-512 if wear is found.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, superseding HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above. Contingency only, if the seal is disturbed. Gland torque 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency only, if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart, because the vibration is treated as in the highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, plus mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A line-break permit is required: drain and vent first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. P-103 is on the filtered-water line, which is dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which is over 25 kg. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair), if wear is found: 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement, contingency only: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 torques. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says pumps from serial HF3-22000 and above must not use HF3-450 and must use cartridge seal HF3-450B with a 30 Nm gland torque. P-103 is serial HF3-22410, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies to this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Figure 3 does not state whether a reading of exactly 7.1 mm/s belongs to Zone C or Zone D. It has been treated conservatively as Zone D (stop). The reliability engineer should confirm the classification.",
    "No non-drive-end vibration reading was reported. The manual requires readings on both housings, with the highest reading used for classification.",
    "It is not stated which housing the 72 C temperature was measured on.",
    "Table 5 fastener torque values are not included in the evidence.",
    "Grease type and correct grease quantity for the bearings are not given in the evidence.",
    "The evidence does not state whether bearing replacement requires removing the back pull-out assembly or disturbing the mechanical seal. This determines whether the seal, sleeve and gasket contingency parts will be needed.",
    "NPSH limits and the method for checking cavitation are not specified in the evidence."
  ]
}
